     According to 18 U.S. Code 1030, if you were to use a buffer overrun attack to commit fraud or related activity in connection with computers, but did not attempt to cause death and did not knowingly or recklessly cause death, then you could receive a maximum penalty of 5 in prison for first offense growing to possibly 20 years.

    According to 18 U.S. Code 1030, if you were to use a buffer overrun attack to commit fraud or related activity in connection with computers, and attempted to cause death or knowingly or recklessly caused death, then you could receive a maximum penalty of life in prison. 


